Today is Saturday morning.
Marine Drive is in South Mumbai.
Today I am going there.
This is my first big outing.
I ask Asha the route.
Asha is my neighbour.
She gives me directions.
"Maya, you go by your daily bus," she says.
"But get down at the main junction."
"From there, board a new bus."
"Where is the new bus stop?" I ask.
"From the junction, go towards the market," Asha says.
"First, walk straight."
"Then, turn left."
"There, board a bus towards the south direction."
"That bus goes towards Marine Drive."
"Thank you, Asha," I say.
I take my bag.
I go towards the bus stop with excitement.
